## 📁 Repository & File Structure

```text
.
├── backend/
│   └── app.py                      # Flask REST API, MySQL DB abstraction, RBAC, & Async Runner
├── frontend/
│   ├── index.html                  # Glassmorphism Single-Page Web Dashboard
│   ├── css/
│   │   └── style.css               # Design System (Colors, Gradients, Cards, Modals)
│   └── js/
│       └── app.js                  # Frontend Controller, API Client, DOM Renderers
├── scripts/
│   └── migrate_sqlite_to_mysql.py  # 1-Click Data Migration Script (SQLite -> MySQL)
├── fetch_keys.yml                  # Optimized Single-Pass SSH Key Discovery Playbook
├── manage_keys.yml                 # SSH Key Lifecycle Management Playbook (Add, Revoke, Disable, Enable)
├── inventory.ini                   # Target Host & Ansible Group Inventory Configuration
├── ansible.cfg                     # Ansible Engine Runtime Flags & Connection Settings
├── run.sh                          # Application Launcher Script (Port 5050)
└── README.md                       # Comprehensive System Architecture Documentation
```

### Key Component Descriptions

* [backend/app.py](file:///Users/mohittiwari/Ansible/backend/app.py): The main application controller containing database initialization (`init_db()`), REST routes, inventory parser, key parsing utilities (`parse_authorized_keys_text()`, `compute_ssh_fingerprint()`), and background threads.
* [fetch_keys.yml](file:///Users/mohittiwari/Ansible/fetch_keys.yml): High-performance Ansible playbook that audits target hosts in a **single shell pass**, reading `/root` and `/home/*` `.ssh/authorized_keys` files and returning Base64 encoded outputs.
* [manage_keys.yml](file:///Users/mohittiwari/Ansible/manage_keys.yml): Safe key management playbook supporting `present` (Add), `absent` (Revoke key), `disable` (Rename `authorized_keys` $\rightarrow$ `.sshmanager_disabled`), and `enable` (Restore from `.sshmanager_disabled`). *Destructive blanket purge operations are explicitly prohibited for safety.*
* [frontend/js/app.js](file:///Users/mohittiwari/Ansible/frontend/js/app.js): Handles real-time search indexing, dynamic access matrix rendering, modal interactions, server metadata editing, and log streaming over REST.

